{"name":"Pink Makeup","hex":"#fc80a5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"makeup","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An item's composition.","Cosmetics; colorants and other substances applied to the skin to alter its appearance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of make up (“ to put makeup on (someone or something)”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/makeup"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cosmetics","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmetics are substances that are intended for application to the body for cleansing, beautifying, promoting attractiveness, or altering appearance. They are mixtures of chemical compounds derived from either natural sources or created synthetically. The products serve various purposes, including personal and skin care. They can also be used to conceal blemishes and enhance natural features. Makeup can add color to the face, enhance features, or alter appearance to resemble a different person, creature, or object."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cosmetics.JPG/330px-Cosmetics.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmetics","wikidata":"Q131207"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/500px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/1280px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/500px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An actor applying bold makeup for a stage performance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelf_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg/500px-Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg/1280px-Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg/500px-Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019